WEBVTT

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:01.962
Oxford Book Worms.

00:00:02.022 --> 00:00:03.923
Stage 1.

00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:05.884
Pocahontas.

00:00:05.944 --> 00:00:09.066
Retold by Tim Vickery.

00:00:09.126 --> 00:00:11.878
Read by Oliver Winen.

00:00:11.938 --> 00:00:25.488
Copyright Oxford University Press 2005.

00:00:25.548 --> 00:00:52.124
Chapter 1 The English in Virginia In January 1607, three ships left England and sailed to America.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.784
There were 150 men on the ships.

00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:07.679
and they wanted to find a new world in the West, a home in a new and exciting country.

00:01:07.739 --> 00:01:16.376
The ships were at sea for four months, and they arrived in Virginia on 26 April 1607.

00:01:16.396 --> 00:01:31.232
After four long months at sea, The men were tired, ill and hungry.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:35.584
But Virginia was beautiful.

00:01:35.644 --> 00:01:46.280
The sky was blue, and they could see rivers and flowers and forests of tall trees.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.806
The Englishmen were very happy.

00:01:50.866 --> 00:01:57.803
But the Algonquin Indians of Virginia were not happy.

00:01:57.862 --> 00:02:03.747
They were afraid of the Englishmen and their ships.

00:02:03.807 --> 00:02:08.740
This is our home, they said.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.104
We don't want these white men here.

00:02:13.164 --> 00:02:16.406
We must fight them.

00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:22.401
But some Indians said, no, wait.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.853
These men are interesting.

00:02:25.913 --> 00:02:31.327
Let's make friends with them and learn about them.

00:02:31.387 --> 00:02:39.868
So the Indians tried to talk to the English men and gave them food to eat.

00:02:39.927 --> 00:02:44.864
The Englishmen gave things to the Indians, too.

00:02:44.924 --> 00:02:50.296
Little knives and pictures and beads.

00:02:50.356 --> 00:02:55.909
The Englishmen began to build a little town.

00:02:55.969 --> 00:03:03.402
They called it Jamestown, because the king of England was called James.

00:03:03.462 --> 00:03:08.553
They called the river James River, too.

00:03:08.613 --> 00:03:18.788
The leaders of the Englishmen were Christopher Newport, Edward Wingfield and John Smith.

00:03:18.848 --> 00:03:32.316
They wanted to learn more about Virginia, so Smith and Newport took twenty men and went up the river in a small boat.

00:03:32.376 --> 00:03:37.900
The other men stayed in Jamestown with Wingfield.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:47.326
They began to build houses and to make gardens and fields outside the town.

00:03:47.386 --> 00:03:54.480
The fields are more important than the houses, said Wingfield.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.793
And we must work quickly, because it's nearly summer now.

00:04:00.853 --> 00:04:06.244
We must have corn and vegetables for the winter.

00:04:06.304 --> 00:04:09.866
But it was not easy.

00:04:09.926 --> 00:04:17.484
The weather was hot, and the men were tired after four months at sea.

00:04:17.544 --> 00:04:20.372
Some men worked hard.

00:04:20.432 --> 00:04:25.439
But many sat in the sun and did nothing.

00:04:25.499 --> 00:04:30.040
The Indians watched and waited.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:37.181
Smith and Newport went a hundred kilometers up the river.

00:04:37.241 --> 00:04:44.123
They visited Indian villages and talked to a lot of Indians.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:51.060
Some of the Indians were friendly, and some were not.

00:04:51.119 --> 00:05:01.678
When Smith and Newport came back to Jamestown, Wingfield was very pleased to see them.

00:05:01.738 --> 00:05:06.400
I was afraid for you, he said.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.490
But you're not dead.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:14.262
No, of course not, said Smith.

00:05:14.322 --> 00:05:16.652
What's the matter?

00:05:16.712 --> 00:05:20.984
It's the Indians, Wingfield said.

00:05:21.044 --> 00:05:23.866
They're trying to kill us.

00:05:23.926 --> 00:05:28.428
Yesterday, they nearly killed me.

00:05:28.488 --> 00:05:31.680
Well, what did you do?"

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.512
Smith asked.

00:05:33.572 --> 00:05:40.441
Our men have guns, and the Indians are very afraid of guns.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:50.190
But there were hundreds of Indians, said Wingfield, and we weren't ready.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:56.423
Our guns were on the ships.

00:05:56.443 --> 00:06:03.136
Why, asked Smith angrily, the men must always be ready.

00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:06.871
They must carry their guns with them.

00:06:06.931 --> 00:06:13.756
The Indians tried to kill you because they weren't afraid of you.

00:06:13.816 --> 00:06:21.768
Yes, but we must be nice to them, said Wingfield.

00:06:21.828 --> 00:06:30.550
We can be friendly, but we must be careful first, said Smith.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:38.818
We must build good walls round the town and put the big guns from the ships on them.

00:06:38.878 --> 00:06:42.871
Then the Indians can't kill us.

00:06:42.931 --> 00:06:47.154
For a month everyone worked hard.

00:06:47.214 --> 00:06:54.450
They built walls round the town and moved the big guns from the ships.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:07:06.550
But the men were afraid to work in the fields because of the Indians, and the sun got hotter and hotter.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:13.727
In June, Newport went back to England with two of the ships.

00:07:13.787 --> 00:07:17.544
105 men stayed in Jamestown.

00:07:17.604 --> 00:07:22.830
They had very little food.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:32.024
The corn from England was now bad, and the new corn in the fields was not ready.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:41.018
The river water was bad too, and soon many of the men were ill with a fever.

00:07:41.078 --> 00:07:45.778
Forty-six men died that summer.

00:07:45.838 --> 00:07:56.709
Some of the men tried to leave Jamestown and go home in the ship, but Smith stopped them.

00:07:56.769 --> 00:08:03.770
We're here to work and to build a new town, he said.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.471
But first we must find food.

00:08:08.531 --> 00:08:20.479
There are birds in the sky, fish in the river, animals in the forest, We must kill them and eat them.

00:08:20.539 --> 00:08:25.230
And we must get corn from the Indians too.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.881
I can do that."

00:08:27.941 --> 00:08:35.893
Smith wasn't afraid of the Indians, but he was always very careful.

00:08:35.953 --> 00:08:40.205
He carried his gun all the time.

00:08:40.265 --> 00:08:47.601
Most of the Indians were afraid of Smith, but they liked him too.

00:08:47.661 --> 00:08:53.526
He was friendly, and he loved their beautiful country.

00:08:53.586 --> 00:09:02.462
And he learned their language because he wanted to talk to them and understand them.

00:09:02.522 --> 00:09:11.419
Often he gave the Indians little things from England, and they gave him food.

00:09:11.479 --> 00:09:20.768
But when winter came, there were only fifty men alive in Jamestown.

00:09:20.828 --> 00:09:26.362
They had some food, but they needed more.

00:09:26.422 --> 00:09:35.962
The Virginian winter is long and cold, and fifty men need a lot of food.

00:09:36.022 --> 00:09:43.558
In December, Smith went up the river in a boat with nine men.

00:09:43.618 --> 00:09:48.052
Two of the friendly Indians went with them.

00:09:48.112 --> 00:09:53.796
It was very cold, and the Englishmen were hungry.

00:09:53.856 --> 00:10:07.686
But Smith was happy and excited I'm going to find food for Christmas," he said to the man in Jamestown.

00:10:07.746 --> 00:10:11.978
Wait for me here, and work hard.

00:10:12.038 --> 00:10:19.349
This is a beautiful country, and we're going to stay here.

00:10:19.409 --> 00:10:54.980
Chapter 2 John Smith and Pocahontas There were a lot of Indian villages in Virginia, and every village had its chief.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.644
But there was only one king.

00:10:59.704 --> 00:11:08.711
That was Powhatan, and he was the king of all the Algonquin Indians.

00:11:08.771 --> 00:11:12.713
Tell me about these white men.

00:11:12.773 --> 00:11:25.318
Powhatan said to his brother, Opekankanu, They are living in my country and killing my people.

00:11:25.378 --> 00:11:29.238
I want to see one of them.

00:11:29.298 --> 00:11:35.491
Powhatan's daughter, Pocahontas, heard this.

00:11:35.551 --> 00:11:39.542
She was thirteen years old.

00:11:39.602 --> 00:11:43.054
What are white men, father?"

00:11:43.114 --> 00:11:44.884
she asked.

00:11:44.944 --> 00:11:48.905
Are they white because they are ill?

00:11:48.965 --> 00:11:52.186
Powhatan smiled.

00:11:52.246 --> 00:11:55.097
No, little Pocahontas.

00:11:55.157 --> 00:11:58.757
They aren't ill, he said.

00:11:58.818 --> 00:12:03.539
They are a new people from over the sea.

00:12:03.599 --> 00:12:08.998
Perhaps we can see and talk to a white man soon.

00:12:09.058 --> 00:12:14.162
My brother is going to find one for us.

00:12:14.222 --> 00:12:23.812
The next day, Opécan Canu went into the forest with two hundred men.

00:12:23.873 --> 00:12:31.574
They found John Smith's nine men next to their boat by the river.

00:12:31.634 --> 00:12:37.532
Smith's men were afraid, and got out their guns.

00:12:37.592 --> 00:12:47.086
But Opé Can Canous men killed two of them, and the other seven ran away.

00:12:47.147 --> 00:12:53.320
John Smith was in the forest with the two Indians.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:13:05.012
When they heard the noise, they ran back to the boat, and saw two hundred men with bows and arrows.

00:13:05.072 --> 00:13:10.193
Then an arrow hit Smith's leg.

00:13:10.253 --> 00:13:19.196
He quickly took out his gun and put a friendly Indian in front of his body.

00:13:19.256 --> 00:13:23.606
What do you want, he asked?

00:13:23.666 --> 00:13:26.827
Don't come near me!

00:13:26.887 --> 00:13:33.621
King Powhatan wants to see you, said Opekancanu.

00:13:33.681 --> 00:13:36.513
Give me your gun."

00:13:36.573 --> 00:13:41.126
No, Smith said at first.

00:13:41.186 --> 00:13:48.493
But there were two hundred Indians, and he was one man.

00:13:48.552 --> 00:13:51.887
So he gave them his gun.

00:13:51.947 --> 00:14:02.531
and went with Ope Kankanu to Werowakamako, the village of King Powhatan.

00:14:02.592 --> 00:14:09.973
In the village, everyone came out to see the Englishman.

00:14:10.033 --> 00:14:15.004
Pocahontas looked at Smith carefully.

00:14:15.064 --> 00:14:18.814
He was very interesting.

00:14:18.874 --> 00:14:22.176
He was not very tall.

00:14:22.236 --> 00:14:25.998
and he had hair on his face.

00:14:26.058 --> 00:14:33.401
Indian men had no hair on their faces, and his eyes.

00:14:33.461 --> 00:14:36.672
His eyes were blue.

00:14:36.732 --> 00:14:41.804
All the men in her village had brown eyes.

00:14:41.864 --> 00:14:47.926
She looked at Smith's blue eyes for a long time.

00:14:47.986 --> 00:14:50.208
They were beautiful.

00:14:50.268 --> 00:14:54.109
the color of the sky.

00:14:54.169 --> 00:15:03.122
Smith smiled at the little girl and closed one of his eyes for a second.

00:15:03.182 --> 00:15:10.774
Pocahontas laughed, and then she smiled back at him.

00:15:10.834 --> 00:15:16.822
Why are you in my country, white man?"

00:15:16.882 --> 00:15:19.437
Powhatan asked.

00:15:19.497 --> 00:15:22.452
Where do you come from?

00:15:22.512 --> 00:15:25.536
Who is your king?

00:15:25.596 --> 00:15:33.851
Smith told him about England and King James and Jamestown.

00:15:33.911 --> 00:15:43.014
It wasn't easy, because he didn't understand Paul Hatton's language very well.

00:15:43.074 --> 00:15:49.094
and Powhatan didn't always understand him.

00:15:49.154 --> 00:15:57.079
We want to live here, and be your friends, Powhatan," he said.

00:15:57.138 --> 00:16:06.654
But this winter the people of Jamestown are hungry, so we need food.

00:16:06.714 --> 00:16:11.196
Opecan Canu was angry.

00:16:11.256 --> 00:16:17.698
These Englishmen cannot live here, he said to his brother.

00:16:17.758 --> 00:16:24.449
They are taking our land and killing our people with their guns.

00:16:24.509 --> 00:16:30.411
They want King James of England to be King here too.

00:16:30.471 --> 00:16:35.140
They call their town King James's town.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:40.612
And they call our beautiful river King James' River.

00:16:40.672 --> 00:16:42.953
But what about us?

00:16:43.013 --> 00:16:46.344
This is our country.

00:16:46.404 --> 00:16:53.969
We live here, and our fathers and grandfathers lived here before us.

00:16:54.028 --> 00:16:59.551
We don't want the English or their King James.

00:16:59.611 --> 00:17:04.269
We must kill them all now.

00:17:04.329 --> 00:17:11.428
Perhaps, Powhaten said, but let's think first.

00:17:11.488 --> 00:17:18.224
The English have guns, so we need guns too.

00:17:18.284 --> 00:17:22.085
I must think carefully about this.

00:17:22.146 --> 00:17:26.378
Pocahontas, come with me."

00:17:26.438 --> 00:17:40.799
They walked into the forest, and Powhaten asked his daughter What do you think about this Englishman, little Pocahontas?

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:44.712
Oh, Father, I like him.

00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:51.516
He has wonderful blue eyes, the color of the sky.

00:17:51.576 --> 00:18:02.838
My brother wants to kill him, but I want to know more about these Englishmen first, and you can help me.

00:18:02.898 --> 00:18:08.226
I'm going to give him to you, little Pocahontas.

00:18:08.286 --> 00:18:11.339
Give him to me, Father."

00:18:11.399 --> 00:18:12.880
Yes.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.722
Listen carefully now.

00:18:15.782 --> 00:18:19.495
You must do this.

00:18:19.555 --> 00:18:24.369
They went back to the village.

00:18:24.429 --> 00:18:30.473
Are we going to kill this white man now, Powhatan?

00:18:30.534 --> 00:18:33.306
Opa Khan Kannu asked.

00:18:33.366 --> 00:18:36.250
"'Yes,' Paohaten said.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:39.352
"'Bring him here.'

00:18:39.412 --> 00:18:47.878
They put John Smith's head on a stone, in front of Paohaten's feet.

00:18:47.938 --> 00:18:56.134
Then Opecan Canu took a big stick and walked to the stone.

00:18:56.194 --> 00:18:59.846
Pocahontas looked at her father.

00:18:59.906 --> 00:19:05.669
He moved his head a little but did not look at her.

00:19:05.729 --> 00:19:11.739
Now, Ope Kan Kanu was next to the stone.

00:19:11.799 --> 00:19:18.874
John Smith closed his eyes and waited to die.

00:19:18.934 --> 00:19:26.331
Suddenly he felt warm arms on his face and head.

00:19:26.391 --> 00:19:36.563
He opened his eyes and saw the face of the young girl with her beautiful dark eyes.

00:19:36.623 --> 00:19:41.434
No, Ope-Kan-Kanu, she cried.

00:19:41.494 --> 00:19:43.064
No!

00:19:43.124 --> 00:19:48.261
I am the king's daughter, and I say no!

00:19:48.321 --> 00:19:51.887
She looked at her father.

00:19:51.948 --> 00:19:55.868
Father, don't kill this man.

00:19:55.928 --> 00:20:00.269
Please, give him to me.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:05.430
At first, Paohatan said nothing.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:09.991
Then, slowly, he smiled.

00:20:10.051 --> 00:20:14.512
Very well, Pocahontas, he said.

00:20:14.572 --> 00:20:18.350
You are only thirteen years old.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:22.017
But this white man is not very big.

00:20:22.077 --> 00:20:25.707
He is a boy with hair on his face.

00:20:25.767 --> 00:20:28.468
You can have him."

00:20:28.528 --> 00:20:35.039
Angrily, Ope Kankanu put his stick down.

00:20:35.099 --> 00:20:37.899
Pocahontas smiled.

00:20:37.919 --> 00:20:42.840
"'Come with me, white man,' she said to him.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.671
"'You are my English man now.

00:20:46.731 --> 00:21:19.362
Come, Chapter 3 A Friend for the English John Smith stayed with Pocahontas for some days.

00:21:19.422 --> 00:21:26.548
She learned some English, and he learned more of her language.

00:21:26.608 --> 00:21:31.241
Soon they were good friends.

00:21:31.301 --> 00:21:40.597
But Paul Hatton's men watched Smith carefully, and he could not leave the village.

00:21:40.657 --> 00:21:57.142
Then, one day, Powhatan said, You can go home to Jamestown, John Smith, but you must give me two of your big guns.

00:21:57.202 --> 00:22:05.336
John Smith did not like this, but he could not say no.

00:22:05.396 --> 00:22:18.153
So he went back to Jamestown, and Pocahontas Opecan Canu and some Indians went with him.

00:22:18.213 --> 00:22:25.025
In Jamestown, Wingfield was not happy.

00:22:25.085 --> 00:22:31.027
We can't give our big guns to the Indians, he said.

00:22:31.087 --> 00:22:36.008
Then they can kill us with our guns.

00:22:36.068 --> 00:22:39.730
It's all right, said Smith.

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.624
Wait.

00:22:41.684 --> 00:22:49.712
He took Opecan Canu and his men to the guns on the town walls.

00:22:49.772 --> 00:22:53.256
Now watch, he said.

00:22:53.316 --> 00:22:59.580
He put some gunpowder and some stones in the gun.

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:09.308
Put your hands over your ears, he said, and look at that tree.

00:23:09.368 --> 00:23:14.301
Pocahontas closed her eyes.

00:23:14.361 --> 00:23:19.792
Then she opened them and looked at the tree.

00:23:19.852 --> 00:23:22.743
It wasn't there.

00:23:22.803 --> 00:23:25.004
What happened?

00:23:25.064 --> 00:23:26.664
She asked.

00:23:26.724 --> 00:23:28.314
Where's the tree?

00:23:28.334 --> 00:23:33.106
I killed it with this gun.

00:23:33.166 --> 00:23:35.036
Smith said.

00:23:35.096 --> 00:23:39.066
He looked at Opé Concanu.

00:23:39.126 --> 00:23:45.136
This gun can kill ten men, Opécancanu.

00:23:45.196 --> 00:23:47.048
Remember that.

00:23:47.108 --> 00:23:51.769
So, take your two guns.

00:23:51.830 --> 00:23:56.082
But the guns were very big.

00:23:56.142 --> 00:24:02.785
And of course, the Indians could not move them.

00:24:02.845 --> 00:24:07.287
Look, said Smith.

00:24:07.347 --> 00:24:11.969
You can't carry these guns through the forest.

00:24:12.029 --> 00:24:17.271
But I can give you some gunpowder for Powhatan.

00:24:17.331 --> 00:24:19.942
Here, take it.

00:24:20.002 --> 00:24:23.854
Be very careful with it.

00:24:23.914 --> 00:24:28.855
Thank you, Ope Kankanu said.

00:24:28.915 --> 00:24:33.962
But one day we want these big guns too.

00:24:34.022 --> 00:24:37.652
They are very important for us.

00:24:37.712 --> 00:24:50.289
Perhaps, said Smith, but we want to be your friends, and friends are better than guns.

00:24:50.350 --> 00:25:01.669
That winter, Pocahontas came to Jamestown every week with food for the Englishmen.

00:25:01.729 --> 00:25:08.064
She learned many interesting things in Jamestown.

00:25:08.124 --> 00:25:12.118
Look at this, Pocahontas.

00:25:12.178 --> 00:25:15.400
John Smith said one day.

00:25:15.461 --> 00:25:19.124
He had a compass in his hand.

00:25:19.184 --> 00:25:21.218
What is it?

00:25:21.278 --> 00:25:23.791
Pocahontas asked.

00:25:23.851 --> 00:25:31.104
She tried to put her finger on the arrow in the compass, but she couldn't.

00:25:31.164 --> 00:25:33.185
It's a compass.

00:25:33.245 --> 00:25:40.118
The arrow always points to the north, Smith said.

00:25:40.178 --> 00:25:42.769
Where is the north?

00:25:42.830 --> 00:25:44.820
Do you know?

00:25:44.880 --> 00:25:47.462
Of course I know.

00:25:47.522 --> 00:25:50.730
All my people know that.

00:25:50.790 --> 00:25:53.429
Well, look.

00:25:53.489 --> 00:25:58.612
The arrow in the compass knows it, too.

00:25:58.672 --> 00:26:03.524
Why can't I put my finger on it?

00:26:03.584 --> 00:26:06.136
Smith smiled.

00:26:06.196 --> 00:26:08.607
Because of the glass.

00:26:08.668 --> 00:26:15.366
You can see through glass, but you can't put your finger through it.

00:26:15.426 --> 00:26:25.514
Yes, she said slowly, but what is a compass for?

00:26:25.574 --> 00:26:32.676
It helps us in our ships when we can't see the sky, he said.

00:26:32.736 --> 00:26:35.297
Which way do we go?

00:26:35.357 --> 00:26:37.498
Where is the north?

00:26:37.558 --> 00:26:41.772
The compass tells us all that.

00:26:41.832 --> 00:26:47.268
Pocahontas was interested in everything.

00:26:47.328 --> 00:26:58.434
She loved to talk to John Smith, and she learned many things about England and the English.

00:26:58.494 --> 00:27:08.763
In March and April 1608, two more ships came to Jamestown.

00:27:08.823 --> 00:27:13.928
Powhatan asked Pocahontas about them.

00:27:13.989 --> 00:27:18.791
How many Englishmen are there now?

00:27:18.851 --> 00:27:20.682
He asked.

00:27:20.742 --> 00:27:31.928
There were thirty-eight before the ships came farther, but now there are about a hundred and fifty.

00:27:31.988 --> 00:27:34.600
It's spring now.

00:27:34.660 --> 00:27:41.638
They must sow corn and vegetables in their fields Are they doing that?

00:27:41.698 --> 00:27:47.270
Yes, Father, but they aren't very good at it.

00:27:47.330 --> 00:27:50.953
This is a new country for them.

00:27:51.013 --> 00:27:54.776
They don't understand it.

00:27:54.836 --> 00:27:58.888
But they must have corn.

00:27:58.948 --> 00:28:02.180
Powhatan was angry.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:05.740
They need food for the winter.

00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:16.721
We can't give them our corn every year, and we kill animals, birds, and fish for our food.

00:28:16.781 --> 00:28:21.212
The English must learn to do that too.

00:28:21.272 --> 00:28:32.966
They are learning, Father, Pocahontas said, but most of these men come from towns in England.

00:28:33.026 --> 00:28:48.734
They don't know about these things, Well, they live here now, so they must learn, said Paohaten, or they must give me guns.

00:28:48.794 --> 00:28:55.400
We have a lot of food in our village, but we need guns.

00:28:55.460 --> 00:29:03.449
I can give the Englishmen food, but they must give me guns first.

00:29:03.509 --> 00:29:08.876
Tell that to your English friends, Pocahontas.

00:29:08.936 --> 00:29:40.600
Chapter 4 A Wife for John Smith But the English didn't want to give Powhatan any guns.

00:29:40.660 --> 00:29:45.914
Oh, no, Pocahontas, John Smith said.

00:29:45.974 --> 00:29:51.209
Your father has thousands of men, but we have only 150.

00:29:51.229 --> 00:29:54.640
We can't give him guns.

00:29:54.700 --> 00:30:04.074
Later, some of Powhatan's men tried to take guns from the English.

00:30:04.134 --> 00:30:07.726
Smith was very angry.

00:30:07.786 --> 00:30:14.728
He locked the men in a little room in Jamestown for a week.

00:30:14.788 --> 00:30:20.270
Then he talked to Pocahontas about them.

00:30:20.330 --> 00:30:27.614
I'm very angry with these men, Pocahontas, he said.

00:30:27.674 --> 00:30:37.700
But I'm not going to kill them, because your father didn't kill me in where a wokomoko.

00:30:37.760 --> 00:30:41.482
I'm going to give them to you.

00:30:41.542 --> 00:30:45.504
Take them home, Pocahontas.

00:30:45.564 --> 00:30:53.278
Pocahontas liked the English, and she often visited Jamestown.

00:30:53.338 --> 00:30:58.880
John Smith liked to teach her new things.

00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:08.181
The sun, Pocahontas, he said one evening, is a red ball in the sky.

00:31:08.241 --> 00:31:12.732
This world is a big round ball, too.

00:31:12.792 --> 00:31:23.106
Thirty years ago, an English man called Francis Drake sailed round the world in a ship.

00:31:23.166 --> 00:31:29.202
Pocahontas laughed, but that's not true.

00:31:29.262 --> 00:31:32.750
Of course the world isn't a ball.

00:31:32.810 --> 00:31:36.494
Why does the sea stay on it then?"

00:31:36.554 --> 00:31:39.586
Smith smiled.

00:31:39.646 --> 00:31:42.309
Oh, I can tell you.

00:31:42.369 --> 00:31:44.230
Listen.

00:31:44.290 --> 00:31:50.586
He talked well, so it was easy to understand him.

00:31:50.646 --> 00:31:57.670
Pocahontas listened and watched his beautiful blue eyes.

00:31:57.730 --> 00:32:09.954
She was fourteen years old, and for her John Smith was the most exciting man in the world.

00:32:10.014 --> 00:32:14.418
Do you have a wife, John Smith?

00:32:14.478 --> 00:32:16.349
She asked one day.

00:32:16.369 --> 00:32:21.322
No, he said slowly.

00:32:21.382 --> 00:32:24.167
Why do you ask?

00:32:24.227 --> 00:32:37.761
Oh, because one day I must have a husband, and she did not finish, but John Smith understood.

00:32:37.821 --> 00:32:49.864
Pocahontas, he said carefully, You are only fourteen years old, and I'm twenty-eight.

00:32:49.924 --> 00:32:56.710
and the daughter of the king must marry somebody important.

00:32:56.769 --> 00:33:09.824
You are an important man in Jamestown, she said quickly, and my people and your people must learn to be friends.

00:33:09.884 --> 00:33:14.676
A husband and wife can stop.

00:33:14.736 --> 00:33:18.695
He put his finger on her mouth.

00:33:18.755 --> 00:33:32.912
Pocahontas, I like you very much, but I'm not the right husband for you, and I don't know a lot about women.

00:33:32.972 --> 00:33:37.696
I can teach you about that," she said.

00:33:37.756 --> 00:33:42.428
He looked at her in surprise and laughed.

00:33:42.489 --> 00:33:46.171
She was angry when he laughed.

00:33:46.231 --> 00:33:49.469
I'm nearly fifteen.

00:33:49.529 --> 00:33:56.418
In my village, a girl can have a husband when she is fifteen.

00:33:56.478 --> 00:33:59.930
Why are you laughing?"

00:33:59.990 --> 00:34:03.641
I'm sorry, he said.

00:34:03.701 --> 00:34:13.830
You are a beautiful, interesting girl, Pocahontas, but you are only a child.

00:34:13.890 --> 00:34:17.166
I'm not a child.

00:34:17.226 --> 00:34:27.290
You're afraid of me, because I'm a king's daughter, and I want you for my husband."

00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:32.863
Pocahontas was angry and unhappy.

00:34:32.923 --> 00:34:37.598
She went away, back to her father's village.

00:34:37.658 --> 00:34:43.676
And she didn't visit John Smith again for two months.

00:34:43.736 --> 00:34:48.739
But she thought about him every day.

00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:58.046
There was only one man in the world for Pocahontas, and that was John Smith.

00:34:58.107 --> 00:35:07.567
And in Jamestown, perhaps John Smith thought about Pocahontas too.

00:35:07.627 --> 00:35:25.683
Chapter 5 Where is John Smith?

00:35:25.744 --> 00:35:52.799
In the winter of 1608, the English in Jamestown were hungry again, so John Smith went to Werowakomoko and asked Powhatan for corn.

00:35:52.860 --> 00:36:08.867
He took many beautiful glass beads with him, because the Indians loved these things, but Powhatan wanted more than beads.

00:36:08.927 --> 00:36:29.774
You can have corn, he said, but you must build one of your big English houses for me, with windows of glass, and you must give me some guns.

00:36:29.834 --> 00:36:35.034
A house, yes, said Smith.

00:36:35.094 --> 00:36:45.883
Tomorrow my men can bring things from Jamestown and begin to build a house for you.

00:36:45.943 --> 00:36:47.884
But guns?

00:36:47.944 --> 00:36:49.196
No.

00:36:49.256 --> 00:36:53.669
Friends do not need guns.

00:36:53.729 --> 00:37:03.158
Paul Hatton smiled, but he was angry very angry.

00:37:03.218 --> 00:37:08.600
Yes, we are friends, he said.

00:37:08.660 --> 00:37:14.023
Tonight you must stay here and eat with us.

00:37:14.083 --> 00:37:19.258
Tomorrow you can have your corn.

00:37:19.318 --> 00:37:26.582
That night, Pocahontas came to John Smith.

00:37:26.642 --> 00:37:29.543
She was afraid.

00:37:29.603 --> 00:37:34.814
My father is angry, she said.

00:37:34.874 --> 00:37:40.066
He wants to kill you and all your men.

00:37:40.126 --> 00:37:43.803
You must be careful.

00:37:43.863 --> 00:37:48.741
John Smith took her hands.

00:37:48.801 --> 00:37:54.753
What a good friend you are, Pocahontas, he said.

00:37:54.813 --> 00:37:58.384
How can I thank you?

00:37:58.444 --> 00:38:04.316
Pocahontas looked into his blue eyes.

00:38:04.376 --> 00:38:09.567
You are my king, she said quietly.

00:38:09.627 --> 00:38:26.646
My king, now and always, So Smith and his men carried their guns all the time, and they watched very carefully.

00:38:26.706 --> 00:38:35.252
The next morning, Opecan Canu and his women came with the corn.

00:38:35.312 --> 00:38:42.335
There is your corn, Opecan Canu said.

00:38:42.395 --> 00:38:45.484
Give us your guns!"

00:38:45.544 --> 00:38:47.286
he smiled.

00:38:47.346 --> 00:38:50.088
Look behind you.

00:38:50.149 --> 00:39:00.806
Smith looked, and 700 Indians came out of the forest with bows and arrows.

00:39:00.866 --> 00:39:21.285
How can ten men fight 700 In a second, John Smith had his hand in Ope Kankanu's hair and his gun in Ope Kankanu's face.

00:39:21.345 --> 00:39:32.347
My gun can kill you, he said angrily, before an arrow can get to me.

00:39:32.407 --> 00:39:36.661
He looked at Ope Kankanu's men.

00:39:36.721 --> 00:39:41.345
Do you want Opecan Canu to die?"

00:39:41.405 --> 00:39:43.236
he called.

00:39:43.296 --> 00:39:48.217
The Indians were afraid of John Smith.

00:39:48.277 --> 00:39:55.479
To them he was a king, and it is not easy to kill a king.

00:39:55.539 --> 00:40:02.461
They put down their bows and arrows and went away into the forest.

00:40:02.521 --> 00:40:17.464
Opecan Canu too was afraid His women put the corn in Smith's boat, and Smith and his men went back down the river to Jamestown.

00:40:17.524 --> 00:40:23.706
Powhatan and Opecan Canu were angry.

00:40:23.766 --> 00:40:31.450
We don't want these Englishmen in our country, Powhatan said.

00:40:31.510 --> 00:40:34.192
We must kill them.

00:40:34.252 --> 00:40:37.037
Kill them all.

00:40:37.097 --> 00:40:41.823
No, Father," said Pocahontas.

00:40:41.883 --> 00:40:46.026
We must learn to be friends with the English.

00:40:46.086 --> 00:40:52.859
John Smith says, Be quiet, Powhatan said.

00:40:52.919 --> 00:40:56.261
John Smith is our enemy.

00:40:56.321 --> 00:40:58.522
Stay away from him.

00:40:58.582 --> 00:41:01.394
Do you understand?

00:41:01.454 --> 00:41:05.316
But you gave him to me, Father.

00:41:05.376 --> 00:41:07.552
Do you remember?

00:41:07.612 --> 00:41:14.012
I loved his blue eyes, then, and I love them now.

00:41:14.072 --> 00:41:17.966
I cannot stay away from him."

00:41:18.026 --> 00:41:26.014
Pocahontas did visit John Smith after that, but not very often.

00:41:26.074 --> 00:41:28.774
It wasn't easy for her.

00:41:28.834 --> 00:41:38.706
There was often fighting between the English and the Indians now, and dead men do not make friends.

00:41:38.766 --> 00:41:46.850
More ships and more men came from England and more guns.

00:41:46.910 --> 00:41:54.723
Jamestown was now a town of 500 people, 500 hungry people.

00:41:54.783 --> 00:42:06.166
The English wanted the Indians corn, and the Indians wanted the Englishman's guns.

00:42:06.226 --> 00:42:18.608
One day, in October 1609, Pocahontas went to Jamestown, but she could not find John Smith.

00:42:18.668 --> 00:42:21.179
Where is he?

00:42:21.240 --> 00:42:24.438
She asked some Englishmen.

00:42:24.498 --> 00:42:26.227
Smith?

00:42:26.287 --> 00:42:29.858
He left Jamestown a month ago.

00:42:29.918 --> 00:42:31.819
One man said.

00:42:31.879 --> 00:42:36.440
He had a bad accident with some gunpowder.

00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:38.951
He was very ill.

00:42:39.011 --> 00:42:42.792
So he went home to England.

00:42:42.852 --> 00:42:44.342
Ill?

00:42:44.402 --> 00:42:46.373
Pocahontas said.

00:42:46.433 --> 00:42:49.394
John Smith is ill?

00:42:49.454 --> 00:42:52.734
Yes, the man said.

00:42:52.794 --> 00:42:59.864
It was a very bad accident and six weeks on a ship.

00:42:59.924 --> 00:43:05.046
Perhaps he's dead now.

00:43:05.106 --> 00:43:08.316
Did he leave a letter for me?

00:43:08.376 --> 00:43:11.036
Pocahontas asked.

00:43:11.096 --> 00:43:13.757
The man laughed.

00:43:13.817 --> 00:43:17.228
A letter for you, little girl.

00:43:17.288 --> 00:43:19.848
But you can't read.

00:43:19.908 --> 00:43:21.249
Why?

00:43:21.309 --> 00:43:23.577
Is it important?

00:43:23.637 --> 00:43:26.756
No, she said.

00:43:26.816 --> 00:43:29.197
It's not important.

00:43:29.257 --> 00:43:33.238
But of course it was.

00:43:33.299 --> 00:43:40.802
She went away into the forest and cried for a long time.

00:43:40.862 --> 00:43:44.114
Where was John Smith?

00:43:44.174 --> 00:43:51.770
Her Englishman with blue eyes, the color of the sky.

00:43:51.830 --> 00:44:23.262
Chapter 6 A Husband for Pocahontas For four years after that, Things were very bad.

00:44:23.322 --> 00:44:40.314
Sometimes Pocahontas tried to help the English, but to Powhatan and Opekonkanu, the English were enemies, and they wanted to kill them all.

00:44:40.375 --> 00:44:45.638
Powhatan gave the English no more corn.

00:44:45.698 --> 00:44:53.182
His men came at night to Jamestown, and took guns and other things.

00:44:53.242 --> 00:45:03.207
When they found Englishmen in the forest, or by the river, they killed them, and took their guns.

00:45:03.267 --> 00:45:11.601
And so, Powhatan now had many guns in Wheroa comical.

00:45:11.661 --> 00:45:19.114
The new leaders of Jamestown were very unhappy about this.

00:45:19.174 --> 00:45:22.797
How can we stop Powhatan?

00:45:22.857 --> 00:45:24.208
They said.

00:45:24.268 --> 00:45:29.317
We must get those guns back from him.

00:45:29.378 --> 00:45:37.440
We need to take a hostage," said a man called Samuel Argo.

00:45:37.500 --> 00:45:47.558
One of the chiefs, or somebody important from Powhatan's family, then we can talk to Powhatan.

00:45:47.618 --> 00:45:56.855
We can give him back the hostage when he gives us the guns, but not before.

00:45:56.915 --> 00:46:00.744
Powhatan has a daughter.

00:46:00.804 --> 00:46:04.494
Pocahontas, said an older man.

00:46:04.554 --> 00:46:10.068
He loves her very much, they say.

00:46:10.128 --> 00:46:17.603
In 1613 Pocahontas was 19.

00:46:17.663 --> 00:46:24.538
She lived now with her father's friend Ayapassus and his wife.

00:46:24.598 --> 00:46:28.710
Ayapassus was friendly with the English.

00:46:28.770 --> 00:46:33.521
And so it was easy for Samuel Argo.

00:46:33.581 --> 00:46:39.842
He came to Ayapasas' village in his ship.

00:46:39.902 --> 00:46:47.344
I have many beautiful things from England in my ship.

00:46:47.404 --> 00:46:53.196
He told Ayapasas, they are all for you.

00:46:53.256 --> 00:46:58.238
But first, you must give me something.

00:46:58.298 --> 00:47:05.746
You must bring Pocahontas onto my ship and leave her here.

00:47:05.806 --> 00:47:15.726
So Iapassus took Pocahontas onto the ship and Argo locked her in a room.

00:47:15.786 --> 00:47:20.404
Pocahontas was very angry.

00:47:20.464 --> 00:47:29.404
I'm sorry," Argle said to her, but you must come with me to Jamestown.

00:47:29.464 --> 00:47:37.028
Your father must stop fighting us, and he must give us back our guns.

00:47:37.089 --> 00:47:40.962
Then you can go home.

00:47:41.022 --> 00:47:47.536
So Pocahontas went to Jamestown and stayed there.

00:47:47.596 --> 00:47:51.924
At first Powhatan was angry.

00:47:51.984 --> 00:47:54.646
He wanted his daughter.

00:47:54.706 --> 00:48:03.954
But then he looked at his guns, and he wanted them more than his daughter.

00:48:04.014 --> 00:48:12.250
We can kill the English with these guns," he said to Opécan Canu.

00:48:12.310 --> 00:48:15.632
Pocahontas likes the English.

00:48:15.692 --> 00:48:23.235
She can stay in Jamestown, and the guns can stay here.

00:48:23.295 --> 00:48:33.860
There were many women in Jamestown now, and Pocahontas soon made new friends.

00:48:33.920 --> 00:48:38.273
The English women liked her very much.

00:48:38.333 --> 00:48:47.468
She stayed in their houses, played with their children, and spoke English all the time.

00:48:47.528 --> 00:48:58.723
After some months, one of her new friends asked her, Are you happy here with us, Pocahontas?

00:48:58.783 --> 00:49:03.010
Would you like to go home to your people?

00:49:03.070 --> 00:49:08.928
The English are my people now, said Pocahontas.

00:49:08.988 --> 00:49:15.502
But perhaps one day your father, said her friend.

00:49:15.562 --> 00:49:23.766
My father, said Pocahontas, likes his guns better than his daughter.

00:49:23.826 --> 00:49:27.008
They are more important to him.

00:49:27.068 --> 00:49:34.443
This is my home now, and I am very happy here.

00:49:34.503 --> 00:49:41.266
One of her new friends was a man called John Roth.

00:49:41.326 --> 00:49:44.288
Pocahontas liked him.

00:49:44.348 --> 00:49:49.270
Roth was a tall man with brown eyes.

00:49:49.330 --> 00:49:56.293
He liked Pocahontas, too, and visited her nearly every day.

00:49:56.353 --> 00:50:02.861
He smiled a lot, and often laughed happily.

00:50:02.921 --> 00:50:13.324
One day, he said, Pocahontas, I have something important to say to you.

00:50:13.384 --> 00:50:22.660
We are good friends, I think, and, well, We can be more than friends.

00:50:22.720 --> 00:50:36.543
I need a wife, Pocahontas, and you are the most beautiful woman in Jamestown, and the most interesting woman too.

00:50:36.603 --> 00:50:43.015
I love you, Pocahontas, and I want to marry you."

00:50:43.075 --> 00:50:48.603
At first, Pocahontas didn't say anything.

00:50:48.663 --> 00:51:01.314
John Rolf was a nice man, but a long time ago, she remembered, she wanted to be the wife of a different John.

00:51:01.374 --> 00:51:07.716
But I'm never going to see John Smith again, she thought.

00:51:07.776 --> 00:51:09.687
He's dead.

00:51:09.747 --> 00:51:13.541
I must forget about him.

00:51:13.601 --> 00:51:18.026
She smiled at John Rolf.

00:51:18.086 --> 00:51:26.762
Yes, John, she said, I would very much like to be your wife.

00:51:26.822 --> 00:51:40.642
And so, on the 5th April, 1614, an Indian girl married an Englishman in the church in Jamestown.

00:51:40.703 --> 00:51:50.856
Pocahontas' father did not come But Opé Concanou was there, with many of her people.

00:51:50.917 --> 00:51:54.908
Your father is happy for you."

00:51:54.968 --> 00:51:57.949
Opé Concanou told her.

00:51:58.009 --> 00:52:01.540
Pocahontas was happy too.

00:52:01.600 --> 00:52:10.773
John Rolf was a good husband, and a year later they had a little son, Thomas.

00:52:10.833 --> 00:52:16.191
Pocahontas loved him very much.

00:52:16.251 --> 00:52:48.163
Chapter 7 England In 1616, Pocahontas John Rolf and their son went to England.

00:52:48.223 --> 00:52:51.854
Ten of her people came too.

00:52:51.915 --> 00:52:58.486
After seven weeks on the ship they arrived in London.

00:52:58.546 --> 00:53:15.384
How big London is, Pocahontas said, there are hundreds of houses here and thousands of people London was very noisy and exciting.

00:53:15.444 --> 00:53:20.406
Pocahontas was interested in everything.

00:53:20.466 --> 00:53:28.370
She went into the shops and looked at the food and the dresses and the books.

00:53:28.430 --> 00:53:37.806
She went up and down the river Thames in a boat and saw the big houses of rich people.

00:53:37.866 --> 00:53:44.432
Every day she saw something new and wonderful.

00:53:44.493 --> 00:53:52.488
But London was very dirty, too, because there were so many people.

00:53:52.549 --> 00:53:57.242
The river was dirty and the water was bad.

00:53:57.303 --> 00:54:03.234
Two of Pocahontas's people were ill and died.

00:54:03.294 --> 00:54:09.294
But Pocahontas was happy and excited.

00:54:09.354 --> 00:54:17.366
Every day she visited big houses and talked to rich and important people.

00:54:17.426 --> 00:54:25.708
Everybody in London wanted to meet her, to talk to her, to be her friend.

00:54:25.768 --> 00:54:39.033
The King and Queen of England heard about John Ross' wife, the Indian girl from Virginia and they wanted to meet her too.

00:54:39.093 --> 00:54:47.015
So one day Pocahontas went to visit King James and Queen Anne.

00:54:47.075 --> 00:54:51.792
They asked her about her father Powhatan.

00:54:51.852 --> 00:54:58.918
My father is the king of the Algonquin people, she said.

00:54:58.978 --> 00:55:08.064
He has many men and villages, but our country is quieter than England.

00:55:08.125 --> 00:55:15.207
Our people understand the forest and the animals and the rivers.

00:55:15.267 --> 00:55:21.069
You can learn from us and we can learn from you too.

00:55:21.129 --> 00:55:24.409
We must be friends.

00:55:24.470 --> 00:55:27.340
Of course we must.

00:55:27.400 --> 00:55:36.672
King James said, Jamestown has my name, so I'm very interested in it.

00:55:36.732 --> 00:55:49.700
They talked for some time, and then his wife, Queen Anne, said, I have a letter about you Pocahontas.

00:55:49.760 --> 00:55:53.893
It's from a man called John Smith.

00:55:53.953 --> 00:56:00.037
He was your friend, he says, when you were a little girl.

00:56:00.097 --> 00:56:02.879
Is that true?

00:56:02.939 --> 00:56:09.878
For a second or two, Pocahontas could not speak.

00:56:09.938 --> 00:56:18.475
Then she said, a letter from John Smith, but he's dead.

00:56:18.535 --> 00:56:21.888
Queen Anne smiled.

00:56:21.948 --> 00:56:23.448
Dead?

00:56:23.508 --> 00:56:27.262
No, he's here in England.

00:56:27.322 --> 00:56:30.934
Look, here is the letter.

00:56:30.995 --> 00:56:35.036
The Queen looked at Pocahontas.

00:56:35.096 --> 00:56:38.406
What's the matter, my dear?

00:56:38.466 --> 00:56:40.776
Are you ill?

00:56:40.836 --> 00:56:45.688
No, no, I'm all right.

00:56:45.748 --> 00:56:48.368
I'm very happy.

00:56:48.428 --> 00:56:54.360
But that night, Pocahontas could not sleep.

00:56:54.420 --> 00:56:57.421
She was very excited.

00:56:57.481 --> 00:57:01.112
John Smith was not dead.

00:57:01.172 --> 00:57:07.978
He was alive, and in England But where?

00:57:08.038 --> 00:57:14.430
Two days later John Smith came to see her.

00:57:14.490 --> 00:57:20.112
He was older, of course, but she remembered him.

00:57:20.172 --> 00:57:28.245
A little man, not tall, but interesting, exciting, alive.

00:57:28.305 --> 00:57:34.201
He smiled at her with those beautiful blue eyes.

00:57:34.261 --> 00:57:38.236
Hello, Pocahontas," he said.

00:57:38.296 --> 00:57:41.048
Do you remember me?

00:57:41.108 --> 00:57:44.318
How could she forget him?

00:57:44.379 --> 00:57:48.720
She looked at him, but said nothing.

00:57:48.780 --> 00:57:52.332
John Rolf watched them.

00:57:52.392 --> 00:57:57.644
It's John Smith, my dear, he said.

00:57:57.704 --> 00:58:00.939
Are you happy to see him?

00:58:00.999 --> 00:58:05.937
But Pocahontas was not happy.

00:58:05.997 --> 00:58:09.210
No, she said.

00:58:09.270 --> 00:58:11.072
I'm sorry.

00:58:11.132 --> 00:58:12.784
No.

00:58:12.844 --> 00:58:17.408
She looked out of the window at nothing.

00:58:17.468 --> 00:58:21.792
She couldn't look at John Smith.

00:58:21.852 --> 00:58:27.704
John Rolf went out, and Smith waited.

00:58:27.764 --> 00:58:36.767
After a minute, he said, You are a wife now, and a mother.

00:58:36.827 --> 00:58:44.770
Yes, Pocahontas looked at him and tried to smile.

00:58:44.830 --> 00:58:47.611
Do I look different?

00:58:47.671 --> 00:58:49.281
He asked.

00:58:49.341 --> 00:58:52.086
I'm older, I know.

00:58:52.147 --> 00:58:58.255
No, you don't look different, she said.

00:58:58.316 --> 00:59:04.720
But why did you go away from Virginia?

00:59:04.780 --> 00:59:09.364
I had an accident, he said.

00:59:09.424 --> 00:59:12.065
I was very ill.

00:59:12.125 --> 00:59:20.256
So I came back to England, and after two years I got better.

00:59:20.316 --> 00:59:25.736
In Jamestown, they told me you were dead.

00:59:25.796 --> 00:59:27.276
Dead?

00:59:27.336 --> 00:59:28.317
No.

00:59:28.377 --> 00:59:30.098
Not me.

00:59:30.158 --> 00:59:33.250
But you didn't tell me.

00:59:33.310 --> 00:59:36.031
You didn't write me a letter.

00:59:36.091 --> 00:59:41.494
Not one letter in eight years, John Smith.

00:59:41.554 --> 00:59:45.496
But you were a child, Pocahontas.

00:59:45.556 --> 00:59:47.860
You couldn't read.

00:59:47.920 --> 00:59:54.386
Well, I can read now," she said angrily.

00:59:54.446 --> 01:00:07.394
Perhaps I was a child, John Smith, but my father gave you to me that day in my father's village long ago.

01:00:07.454 --> 01:00:09.836
Do you remember?

01:00:09.896 --> 01:00:16.244
That day was the beginning of my love for you.

01:00:16.304 --> 01:00:26.906
He looked at her sadly with those beautiful blue eyes, and she was a child again.

01:00:26.966 --> 01:00:30.920
She remembered everything.

01:00:30.980 --> 01:00:35.716
You didn't love me, she said.

01:00:35.776 --> 01:00:38.047
You never loved me.

01:00:38.067 --> 01:00:48.416
I don't know about love," he said slowly.

01:00:48.476 --> 01:00:58.546
You are the daughter of a king, Pocahontas, and I'm not rich or important.

01:00:58.606 --> 01:01:01.318
I never had a wife.

01:01:01.378 --> 01:01:10.236
Perhaps I don't understand women, and you were a child, Pocahontas.

01:01:10.296 --> 01:01:19.878
I was a child, but I loved you, and you went away, she said.

01:01:19.938 --> 01:01:26.040
For eight years I heard nothing from you.

01:01:26.100 --> 01:01:31.352
For a long time he said nothing.

01:01:31.412 --> 01:01:37.724
Then he said, I'm sorry Pocahontas.

01:01:37.784 --> 01:01:40.625
I was wrong.

01:01:40.686 --> 01:01:47.500
I loved you so much," she said sadly.

01:01:47.560 --> 01:01:54.392
Then the door opened and her little son Thomas came in.

01:01:54.453 --> 01:02:04.027
But now I have a son and a husband, she said, and they love me.

01:02:04.087 --> 01:02:08.278
You and I cannot be friends.

01:02:08.338 --> 01:02:12.030
Goodbye, John Smith.

01:02:12.091 --> 01:02:16.144
Goodbye, Pocahontas.

01:02:16.204 --> 01:02:23.089
He looked at her for a minute, and then walked out of the door.

01:02:23.150 --> 01:02:26.793
She never saw him again.

01:02:26.853 --> 01:02:35.893
Six months later, John Rolf said, We must go back to Virginia, my dear.

01:02:35.954 --> 01:02:44.386
My work is waiting for me there, and you need the warm sun of Virginia, too."

01:02:44.446 --> 01:02:46.689
It was true.

01:02:46.749 --> 01:02:49.972
Pocahontas was now ill.

01:02:50.032 --> 01:02:56.536
and the cold rain of the English winter was not good for her.

01:02:56.596 --> 01:03:02.090
But she said nothing and got ready to leave.

01:03:02.150 --> 01:03:11.386
The ship went down the river from London to a town called Graves End, near the sea.

01:03:11.446 --> 01:03:19.937
But when they got there, Pocahontas was very ill, and she could not move.

01:03:19.997 --> 01:03:28.658
John Roth sat by his wife's bed and watched her face sadly.

01:03:28.718 --> 01:03:32.350
She smiled at him.

01:03:32.410 --> 01:03:34.551
Goodbye, John.

01:03:34.571 --> 01:03:44.543
I am going home, home to the forests and rivers of my country.

01:03:44.603 --> 01:03:53.576
Pocahontas died in graves and in March 1617.

01:03:53.636 --> 01:03:57.778
She is famous for two things.

01:03:57.838 --> 01:04:05.242
She was the first American woman to marry an English man and come to England.

01:04:05.302 --> 01:04:12.676
And she was a good friend to the English when they first went to Virginia.

01:04:12.736 --> 01:04:21.429
Her husband, John Roth, went back to Virginia and married an English woman there.

01:04:21.489 --> 01:04:26.682
He died in Virginia in 1622.

01:04:26.742 --> 01:04:40.732
Pocahontas' son, Thomas, lived with the raw family in England when he was a child, but in 1635 he went to live in Virginia.

01:04:40.792 --> 01:04:47.108
John Smith did not leave England again.

01:04:47.168 --> 01:04:56.244
He wrote many interesting books about America, and he wrote about Pocahontas in those books.

01:04:56.304 --> 01:05:03.237
He lived until 1631, but he never had a wife.

01:05:03.298 --> 01:05:15.027
Perhaps he could not forget the sad, dark eyes of Pocahontas when she said goodbye to him for the last time.

